From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:36:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Never hit a box whose transform collapses an axis

hit_inner maps the point into a transformed node through the
transform's inverse. A singular transform (scale(0) along either
axis, as Material's line ripple ::after uses at rest) has no inverse:
kurbo returns NaN coordinates, and every negated bounds check below
treats NaN as inside. The collapsed box then answered for every point
on the page. On Google Flights it sat above every control, so all 71
clicks the agent tried there fell back to the keyboard.

CSS Transforms does not render such a box, so neither it nor its
descendants are hit.
---
 src/node/node.rs | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/node/node.rs b/src/node/node.rs
index a02694a..efb68ce 100644
--- a/src/node/node.rs
+++ b/src/node/node.rs
@@ -1859,6 +1859,12 @@ impl Node {
         let mut y = y - self.final_layout().location.y + self.scroll_offset().y as f32;

         if let Some(t) = self.transform().as_deref() {
+            // A transform that collapses an axis (Material's line ripple: scaleX(0)) maps no
+            // point back. CSS Transforms says such a box is not rendered, so nothing in it is
+            // hit; its inverse is all NaN, and every bounds check below passes a NaN.
+            if t.determinant().abs() <= f64::EPSILON {
+                return None;
+            }
             let p = t.inverse() * kurbo::Point::new(x as f64 * scale, y as f64 * scale);
             x = (p.x / scale) as f32;
             y = (p.y / scale) as f32;
